#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Measure compute, application requests, short commands, native calls and JIT churn.

Use Python 3.11+ and hyperfine 2.x on Linux in a built tree. Python candidates include the stock
arm for classification. The default corpus site is prepared if needed. ORACLE_T, LUCIFER,
PYPY and AWFY_GO name executables (the last is the verified AWFY port). WEB_SITE
contains Flask. TIMING_PREFIX wraps each single-core arm and supplies affinity.
TEST_PREFIX wraps the threaded web section. Optional LUCIFER_PREFIX applies
resource controls per candidate invocation. Profiling needs Linux perf, stock
debug lines and llvm-symbolizer. Supply wrk via WRK or PATH. The scratch run
records the series behind the two summaries. Use --repeatability RUN on a
baseline containing stock and Lucifer to measure empirical paired noise.
"""
